Subject: drop the release check from send and receive, and own /usr/bin/croc-relay

send() and receive() start a background request to api.github.com for
the latest release, which --local does not stop and --quiet only hides;
without the two calls a transfer makes no connection but the transfer's
own. `croc update` stays, and asks only when it is run.

The KDOS package installs the binary as /usr/bin/croc-relay behind a
/usr/bin/croc wrapper. Naming that path beside /usr/bin/croc makes
`croc update` answer, without a network request, that the system package
manager updates it, instead of pointing at the upstream installer.

